</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-aim-hip-and-ads" data-group="Aim" data-title="Hip fire vs aiming down sights" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Aim</p>
    <h1>Hip fire vs aiming down sights</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Give aiming down sights (ADS) its own speed, and match the game's zoom-in time.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-hip-and-ads--ads-aim-tab">
    <h2>The ADS aim tab</h2>
    <p>On the Aim screen, tap <b>ADS aim</b>. By default ADS uses your hip settings. Change them only if ADS feels too fast or too slow.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-aim-basic-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The ADS aim tab. A: the ADS aim tab. B: the ADS Speed stepper reading Same as hip. C: the Activation card, closed, showing No delay.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ADS.1 — Aim, ADS aim tab, mouse config</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>ADS aim</b></td><td>Settings used while you aim down sights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Speed</b> (<b>Same as hip</b>)</td><td>ADS speed. Below 0 = same as hip.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Activation</b></td><td>When the ADS settings take over. Shows <b>No delay</b> when off.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Speed</b> (ADS aim)</td><td data-label="What it does">Turn speed while aiming. "Below 0 = same as hip."</td><td data-label="Range">0–100, step 1; one step below 0 reads <b>Same as hip</b></td><td data-label="Default"><b>Same as hip</b></td><td data-label="Start here">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Tracking while scoped feels slow</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Scoped aim overshoots</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Smoothing</b> (ADS aim)</td><td data-label="What it does">Smoothing while aiming.</td><td data-label="Range"><b>Same as hip</b>, Disabled, Light, Balanced, Heavy, Custom</td><td data-label="Default"><b>Same as hip</b></td><td data-label="Start here">Same as hip</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Scoped aim shakes</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Scoped aim feels floaty</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>The line at the bottom says what ADS takes from Hip, for example <b>Speed and Smoothing are inherited from Hip.</b></p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-hip-and-ads--activation">
    <h2>Activation: match the zoom-in time</h2>
    <p>Most games take a moment to zoom in. During that moment they still turn at hip speed. Activation tells the EXO to wait the same time before switching to your ADS settings.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On the <b>ADS aim</b> tab, tap <b>Activation</b> to open it. It's closed by default.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Activate</b>, tap <b>+</b> to match how long the game takes to zoom in.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Deactivate</b>, set how long it takes to zoom back out.</li>
      <li>Optional: switch on <b>Smooth ADS Transition</b> to blend the change instead of one jump.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-ads-activation.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The ADS aim tab with the Activation card open. 1: the ADS aim tab. 2: the Activation header. 3: Activate at 0 ms. 4: Deactivate at 0 ms. 5: the Smooth ADS Transition help button, with its switch off below.">
      <figcaption>Figure AIM-ADS.2 — Aim, ADS aim, Activation open (EXO connected)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Number</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">1</span></td><td><b>ADS aim</b></td><td>The settings used while you aim down sights.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">2</span></td><td><b>Activation</b></td><td>Tap to open or close this card.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">3</span></td><td><b>Activate</b></td><td>How long the game takes to zoom in.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">4</span></td><td><b>Deactivate</b></td><td>How long the game takes to zoom back out.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">5</span></td><td><b>Smooth ADS Transition</b></td><td>Tap <b>?</b> to read about it; the switch is under it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Activate</b></td><td data-label="What it does">After you start aiming, keep Hip settings this long, then use ADS settings.</td><td data-label="Range">0–1000 ms, step 4</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Aim jumps to ADS speed before the zoom finishes</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">ADS speed kicks in late</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Deactivate</b></td><td data-label="What it does">After you stop aiming, keep ADS settings this long.</td><td data-label="Range">0–1000 ms, step 4</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Hip speed comes back before the zoom-out ends</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Hip aim feels slow after you let go</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Smooth ADS Transition</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Blends from Hip to ADS speed across the Activate time, and back across Deactivate.</td><td data-label="Range">On / Off</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Turn on if the speed change feels like a jolt</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Scripts set to run only while aiming still start the moment you press aim. The delay only changes your aim settings.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-aim-hip-and-ads--related">
